A direct all-hidden fused LayerNorm+projection kernel exceeds shared-memory limits at the useful block sizes. The next viable optimization is masked cases: two benchmark shapes have a random 0/1 mask, and current code still projects every masked-out pair before multiplying by zero. I’ll benchmark the existing sparse-mask path and a couple of alternatives around that.
