The raw `dim=128,N=1024` projection is also already close to its best point: `128x32x64` remains the best among stable candidates. A couple of larger channel blocks compile but are much slower, so I’m avoiding those.
codex
I’m moving to the output LayerNorm/gate/final-linear kernel now. It accounts for about `0.6-1.1 ms` on the large cases, so even modest block-size wins matter for the geometric mean.
