codex
The selected benchmark paths already store the final output as FP16, which explains why the full-profile output kernel was faster than my isolated FP32-output test. The only consistent micro-win I found is `dim=384` LayerNorm using `BLOCK_M=16,num_warps=8`; I’ll patch that in the selected wrappers and run the official evaluator.
