codex
The RMS-style input approximation is not robust for `dim=128`, and the exact `dim=384` variant would only save a tiny operation. A better exact cleanup is in the output LayerNorm: compute variance as `E[x^2] - mean^2` instead of summing `(x-mean)^2`, which matches the input LayerNorm form and removes one vector expression from the hot output kernel.
